        <briefdescription>
<para>Simply computes the gradient of the quadratic cost <formula id="0">$ J(x, u) = \sum_{j=1}^{N-1} \ell_j(x^j, u^j) + \ell_N(x^N) $</formula>, with  <formula id="1">$ \ell_j(x, u) = \tfrac12 \left\| \begin{pmatrix} x - x^j_\text{ref}
\\ u - u^j_\text{ref} \end{pmatrix} \right\|_{H_j}^2 $</formula>, with the Hessian <formula id="2">$ H_j = \begin{pmatrix} Q_j &amp; S_j^\top \\ S_j &amp; R_j \end{pmatrix} $</formula>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Stores <formula id="3">$ \nabla J(0, 0) $</formula> to <computeroutput>qr</computeroutput>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
